# Trivy suppression list.
#
# Keep this file present (workflows pass `--ignorefile .trivyignore`); add new
# suppressions here with a dated `exp:` and a rationale. Each entry must be
# time-boxed so a suppression cannot silently outlive the condition it accepts.
#
# Historical note: the former entries masked docker/docker SDK CVEs reachable
# only through the legacy culvert-updater sidecar module (RISK-ACC-1 / DEBT-008).
# That module was removed, so nothing imports docker/docker and those masks are
# gone.

# CVE-2026-14456 (HIGH) — openssl: DoS via unbounded memory growth in the QUIC
# server, in Alpine's libcrypto3/libssl3. Base image alpine:3.24 ships 3.5.7-r0;
# fixed in 3.5.8-r0. alpine:3.24 is already the newest Alpine release (3.25/3.26
# do not exist yet) and the runtime stage already runs `apk upgrade --no-cache`,
# so there is no base-image bump available — the fix arrives only when Alpine
# publishes 3.5.8-r0 to the 3.24 apk repo, at which point `apk upgrade` remediates
# the actual package and this entry becomes a no-op. Not-exploitable rationale:
# the culvert binary is a static CGO_ENABLED=0 Go build and does not link Alpine's
# libssl, and the appliance runs no OpenSSL QUIC server. Time-boxed risk-acceptance
# (owner-approved) to unblock the Deep gate until the package publishes.
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-09-15
